---
code: resolver-conflict
when-fires: two oracle files declare one kind's resolver. cli/main.rs. `{kind}` = the kind, `{count}` = the resolver count.
why: 24F §3 at-most-one-resolver-per-kind: BOTH refused (never first-wins-silently); the kind keeps token-equality.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- resolver-conflict && mise run loom:promote -- resolver-conflict`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all resolver-conflict` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork install nginx

-- hork.oracle.sh --
#!/usr/bin/env dorc-sh
# dorc-lang/v0.2
hork__predict() {
   pkg : sm.dorc.Package = "$1"
   hork --query "$pkg" >/dev/null 2>&1 : sm.dorc.Package:"$pkg"@installed
}

sm_dorc_Package__resolve() {
   hork --canonical -- "$1"
}

-- wombat.oracle.sh --
#!/usr/bin/env dorc-sh
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# A second author's take on the same kind's identity. One kind, one owner.
sm_dorc_Package__resolve() {
   wombat --canonical -- "$1"
}

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh -o hork.oracle.sh -o wombat.oracle.sh
error[resolver-conflict]: Kind `sm_dorc_Package` has 2 resolvers across the
loaded oracle files, and a kind has one identity, so Dorc refuses them all --
entities of this kind compare by name alone until exactly one `__resolve`
remains.
      [ hork.oracle.sh:8:1
   8 | sm_dorc_Package__resolve() {
     | \______________________/
